 "lines": [],
 "notes": "Plan of the Free French minelaying submarine Rubis (66 x 7.12 m), scuttled in 1958 and upright on flat sand at 40-41 m about 2.6 km SE of Cap Camarat, bow north and stern south (Atlas PALM, DRASSM). Position 43 11.301 N 6 42.038 E from the Port-Cros national park Neptune sheet; features from Joncheray and Brunner via nicoblon.free.fr and Atlas PALM: the stern was blown open and both propellers are gone, the bow overhangs the sand with the tow cable, the conning tower (about 34 m) and gun mounting sit amidships; positions along the hull are approximate. No fixed mooring is published; the site file's point is about 600 m SW of the wreck.",
